      "defect": "citation-inaccurate",
      "evidence": "Step 1.1 cites [F4] to justify unchanged integrals after replacing the shapes by their products with 1_{S\\E_0}. The cited theorem, thm-the-lebesgue-integral-respects-almost-everywhere-equality, states “Let f,g∈L^1(μ),” and def-l-one-of-a-measure defines L^1(μ) using integrable representatives f:X→C. Here the Statement permits shapes into [0,+∞], and [F3] establishes only that they are finite almost everywhere. A shape equal to +∞ at a null point and 1 elsewhere has finite integral but is not such a C-valued representative, so [F4] does not license this application as written. The equality needs justification for extended nonnegative integrands or a citation with that domain.",
